From: liviyifan <344781483+liviyifan@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] [ORC] LLJIT: link AArch64 ILP32 objects with RuntimeDyld

The AArch64 backend of JITLink reads ELF64 objects only. Keep ILP32 on
RuntimeDyld, which handles its ELF32 objects.

Signed-off-by: liviyifan <344781483+liviyifan@users.noreply.github.com>
---
 llvm/lib/ExecutionEngine/Orc/LLJIT.cpp | 3 ++-
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/llvm/lib/ExecutionEngine/Orc/LLJIT.cpp b/llvm/lib/ExecutionEngine/Orc/LLJIT.cpp
index 67bb7dd8a..1575330d9 100644
--- a/llvm/lib/ExecutionEngine/Orc/LLJIT.cpp
+++ b/llvm/lib/ExecutionEngine/Orc/LLJIT.cpp
@@ -807,7 +807,8 @@ Error LLJITBuilderState::prepareForConstruction() {
       UseJITLink = true;
       break;
     case Triple::aarch64:
-      UseJITLink = !TT.isOSBinFormatCOFF();
+      // JITLink reads ELF64 objects only: ILP32 (ELF32) stays on RuntimeDyld.
+      UseJITLink = !TT.isOSBinFormatCOFF() && !TT.isILP32Environment();
       break;
     case Triple::arm:
     case Triple::armeb:
